# Nothing here is required to boot.
# `npm run setup` asks for the Telegram bot, text/image/audio models,
# and the MCP aggregators (Composio, Executor, Upsy, Self-hosted, both, or none) and stores
# them on the volume. Variables below are optional overrides: when set,
# they win over the volume. TZ is the container clock and is not stored
# by setup. Leave a line unset rather than filling in a personal value.

# TZ=UTC

# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHATS=

# Optional WhatsApp numbers (digits, country code, comma-separated). Read only
# when WhatsApp is the gateway chosen in `npm run setup`. Leave unset to use
# the list saved there. A Brazilian mobile matches with or without the extra 9
# after the area code. Not required to boot.
# WHATSAPP_ALLOWED_USERS=15551234567,15557654321

# EXECUTOR_MCP_URL=
# EXECUTOR_TOKEN=
# COMPOSIO_MCP_URL=
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# COMPOSIO_USER_ID=
# Upsy (https://upsy.ai/connect) has no API key and no env var. Choose it in
# npm run setup and paste the browser redirect URL
# (http://127.0.0.1:33418/callback; nothing listens there). Tokens stay in
# the volume credential mcp-upsy.
# Self-hosted gateway. A URL alone turns it on. The token is optional.
# An empty header sends Authorization: Bearer. Another name sends the raw token.
# Executor self-host: <origin>/mcp (local CLI http://127.0.0.1:4312/mcp,
# Docker http://127.0.0.1:4400/mcp). runelay: <origin>/v1/mcp with an rnl_ key.
# SELF_HOSTED_MCP_URL=
# SELF_HOSTED_TOKEN=
# SELF_HOSTED_HEADER=

# Sandbox. Empty until you set one. A machine id is used only when set
# here or in $DATA_DIR/config.yaml. With neither set, discovery uses a
# machine only when exactly one is running.
# INSTABOX_ACCOUNT_ID=
# INSTABOX_MACHINE_ID=
# INSTABOX_REPO_ALLOWLIST=

# Compat reserve only ("Other" in setup). Ignored when an official setup
# is already on the volume.
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# LLM_API_KEY=
# Optional model rows: id or id|contextWindow|maxTokens|reasoning, where
# reasoning is `false`, `true`, or the exact `+` separated level list the
# upstream model accepts. Discovery via GET /models cannot see capabilities,
# so without this, /thinking stays limited to "off". Ollama (host ollama.com,
# port 11434, or a base path containing /api) is probed with POST /api/show;
# a thinking model then offers off/low/medium/high unless this field sets
# reasoning explicitly. off is sent as reasoning_effort "none".
# LLM_MODELS=
